Unhomed gantry coordinate transitions and saved positions
=======================================================

Run with: bash tests/motion/unhomed-gantry/test.sh

These tests compile the actual controller and task-interface sources with
undefined-behavior/bounds checks. They require the LinuxCNC development
headers/libraries, GCC and G++, but do not start LinuxCNC or realtime threads.

The controller test checks joint-to-teleop/coordinated transitions and
re-enabling with either mode already selected, with trivkins identity and
both kinematics types. It verifies continuous motor commands and unchanged
following error after a partial homing coordinate reset or independent joint
movement, including nonzero motor offsets and backlash. Either side may have
finished homing first; its established coordinate is retained. Homed, independent,
and extra joints are excluded; moving/homing transitions are deferred.

The position test uses the actual INI reader and save/load functions. It
checks inline and OPTIONS coordinates, nonstandard joint order, a different
TRAJ axis list, non-trivial kinematics, unused and extra joints, full-size
and oversized mappings, command failures, and all 16 saved position slots.
